{"id":"wallach-blenkiron","title":"London to Cape Town by sidecar: Wallach and Blenkiron","who":"Theresa Wallach & Florence Blenkiron","when":"1934–1935","vehicle":"600 cc Panther with sidecar and trailer","kind":"moto","color":"#b91c1c","media":[{"kind":"book","title":"The Rugged Road","by":"Theresa Wallach","note":"Her account, published in 2001"}],"summary":"Two young British engineers and racers ride a Panther with sidecar and trailer from London across the Sahara, reportedly without a compass, and down through Central and East Africa to Cape Town: about 13,500 miles in nearly eight months, through heat, wild animals, breakdowns and politics. Seen off by Lady Astor and five women MPs.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Theresa Wallach","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theresa_Wallach"},{"label":"Historic UK: Florence Blenkiron and Theresa Wallach","url":"https://www.historic-uk.com/CultureUK/Florence-Blenkiron-Theresa-Wallach-Motorcyclists/"},{"label":"National Motor Museum: on a Panther through Africa","url":"https://nationalmotormuseum.org.uk/story-of-motoring/motoring-topics/international-womens-day-and-womens-history-month/on-a-panther-through-africa/"}],"approximate":"Few places are recorded: El Goléa on New Year's Day 1935, and the towns Blenkiron listed on her sidecar on the way back. The line between them is approximate.","km":14377,"bbox":[-2.2076,-33.9287,34.9721,51.5132],"stops":[{"name":"London","place":"Aldwych, London","at":[51.5132,-0.1171],"date":"11 Dec 1934","text":"Away from Crown House, Aldwych, seen off by Lady Astor."},{"name":"El Goléa","place":"El Goléa, Algeria","at":[30.5837,2.8831],"date":"1 Jan 1935","text":"New Year in the Sahara, deep in Algeria."},{"name":"Bangassou","place":"Bangassou, Central African Republic","at":[4.7435,22.8233],"text":"Through the forests of Central Africa."},{"name":"Kampala","place":"Kampala, Uganda","at":[0.3177,32.5814],"text":"Into East Africa."},{"name":"Kakamega","place":"Kakamega, Kenya","at":[0.4957,34.8015],"text":"Kenya."},{"name":"Salisbury","place":"Harare, Zimbabwe","at":[-17.8567,31.0602],"text":"Better roads for the last 3,000 miles, through Rhodesia."},{"name":"Bloemfontein","place":"Bloemfontein, South Africa","at":[-29.1164,26.2155],"text":"South Africa."},{"name":"Cape Town","place":"Cape Town, South Africa","at":[-33.9288,18.4172],"date":"29 Jul 1935","text":"Cape Town, nearly eight months after London. Blenkiron rode back alone, home in April 1936."}],"legs":[{"by":"ride","km":2132,"line":[[51.5132,-0.1171],[51.4993,-0.1431],[51.4762,-0.1487],[51.4357,-0.256],[51.3976,-0.2459],[51.3747,-0.3149],[51.3513,-0.3307],[51.3299,-0.4401],[51.2821,-0.5041],[51.2468,-0.5944],[51.2134,-0.648],[51.1681,-0.6587],[51.1471,-0.7035],[51.1142,-0.7202],[51.0729,-0.8762],[51.0561,-0.9033],[51.0312,-0.9091],[51.0117,-0.9523],[50.9319,-0.9953],[50.8464,-1.0124],[50.837,-1.0803],[50.8134,-1.0855],[50.8075,-1.1133],[50.6856,-1.027],[49.6695,-1.5903],[49.6497,-1.6162],[49.6356,-1.5765],[49.588,-1.5967],[49.5472,-1.5594],[49.4992,-1.4828],[49.4745,-1.3691],[49.3417,-1.2717],[49.2951,-1.1663],[49.2256,-1.1236],[49.124,-1.1782],[49.0812,-1.032],[49.0158,-0.9688],[48.9785,-0.9527],[48.8452,-1.248],[48.7481,-1.2812],[48.6854,-1.3746],[48.5926,-1.3289],[48.513,-1.3483],[48.4214,-1.3127],[48.3342,-1.3001],[48.157,-1.6004],[48.1157,-1.5745],[48.0816,-1.6755],[47.9807,-1.6958],[47.9314,-1.6727],[47.8461,-1.6963],[47.7984,-1.6896],[47.7476,-1.7154],[47.688,-1.7003],[47.6044,-1.628],[47.3351,-1.6532],[47.2645,-1.5882],[47.2674,-1.5621],[47.2297,-1.4695],[47.1721,-1.5168],[47.1387,-1.5123],[47.052,-1.4161],[46.8554,-1.279],[46.8338,-1.2278],[46.7537,-1.1674],[46.6024,-1.1382],[46.5341,-1.0753],[46.4366,-0.834],[46.3914,-0.6652],[46.4289,-0.5221],[46.419,-0.4097],[46.3554,-0.3374],[46.3455,-0.3017],[46.2878,-0.3924],[46.1693,-0.5105],[46.1104,-0.5349],[45.9412,-0.5587],[45.8804,-0.621],[45.8358,-0.6277],[45.8166,-0.6513],[45.7602,-0.6722],[45.6483,-0.6318],[45.5982,-0.5897],[45.4725